# pot: the DB8E shows the pot's value when the pot moves (issue #19).
# Spec: pot.md "the `pot` circuit automatically updates the display whenever the
# input pot value has changed. It outputs the updated value of `output`" — the
# SCALED output, and only `output` ("If you use other outputs like
# `lefthalfinv` etc., these outputs are not being displayed").
# The header is the automatic one derived from the `output` target: a register,
# so "Output O1" (hardware.md §6.12's own pot example).
#   t0: seeded at startvalue 0.3 -> 0.3*2 + 1 = 1.6, but nothing has MOVED yet,
#       so the screen stays off.
#   t1: pot to 0.5 -> 0.5*2 + 1 = 2.0
#   t2: unchanged  -> the screen holds 2.0
#   t3: pot to 1.0 -> 1.0*2 + 1 = 3.0
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[p2b8]
[db8e]

[pot]
    pot          = P1.1
    startvalue   = 0.3
    outputscale  = 2
    outputoffset = 1
    output       = O1
>>>
@0 set P1.1 0.3
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 set P1.1 0.5
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 2.0 tol 1e-5
@1 expectdisplay D1 header "Output O1"
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 2.0 tol 1e-5
@3 set P1.1 1.0
@3 expectdisplay D1 value 3.0 tol 1e-5
